WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.190
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:01.952 --> 00:00:04.531
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Holidays together are never a good idea.

00:00:04.873 --> 00:00:07.652
Believe me, I know. <b>I’ve been there.</b>

00:00:08.136 --> 00:00:10.869
And I have a trail of broken friendships to prove it.

00:00:12.838 --> 00:00:13.528
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:14.396 --> 00:00:17.656
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> You’re looking forward to relaxing on the beach with Joanna Trollope’s latest

00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:24.129
must-read novel, while their mission is to visit every ancient ruin within a 50-mile radius.

00:00:24.344 --> 00:00:27.387
Which is all fine if they don’t mind <b>going it alone,</b>

00:00:27.751 --> 00:00:32.637
but when they try to make you feel guilty for lying on your lounger, it’s a different story.

00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:35.364
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:39.607
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Now, I’m not really a camping kind of girl,

00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:43.157
but since this motorhome was like the Waldorf on wheels,

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.020
and North American campsites are known for all their <b>mod cons,</b>

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.480
I thought that I’d be pretty safe.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.056
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.515
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> …a week with someone else’s hyperactive toddler is enough

00:00:56.515 --> 00:01:00.501
to turn even the most mild-mannered of us into Supernanny.

00:01:01.023 --> 00:01:04.413
And you try packing your own children off to bed at a reasonable hour

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.184
when theirs are still <b>bouncing off the ceiling</b> at midnight,

00:01:07.184 --> 00:01:09.662
<b>hyped up on</b> fizzy drinks and video games.

00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:12.376
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:01:13.146 --> 00:01:15.044
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I once spent a week in France,

00:01:15.044 --> 00:01:20.285
breastfeeding my newborn daughter in a wardrobe because our child-free friends

00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:24.083
hadn’t allowed for the vast amount of baggage a baby comes with

00:01:24.257 --> 00:01:27.028
and had allocated us the smallest room.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.439
And they were <b>most put out</b> that we couldn’t drop everything

00:01:30.582 --> 00:01:33.706
and <b>hit the town</b> at night, like in the old days.